From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-16
Subject: [PATCH jm-v7 003] kbase: skip MEM_JIT_INIT on Bifrost JM, GROW_ON_GPF tiler heap with 1 MiB commit biblioklept

Purpose: KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_JIT_INIT fails with ENOMEM on G52 r1 kernels.
Nothing panvk allocates on JM needs JIT or CUSTOM_VA (CSF tiler heap
contexts are the only kernel-internal users), so for JM arch < 9 skip the
ioctl and log "v%u JM, KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_JIT_INIT skipped". Arch is read
from the gpuprops buffer already fetched (RAW_GPU_ID, else PRODUCT_ID).
The JM tiler heap and indirect varying buffer are already GROW_ON_GPF
(PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_ALLOC_ON_FAULT, 2 MiB extension); on arch < 9 the
GPU-only ones now commit 1 MiB up front (JV: 256 pages) and log the
committed/VA pages. v9 keeps JIT_INIT and its TILER_ALIGN_TOP path.
Source/Reference: JimVulkan/mali-panvk src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
(MIT, no JIT, GROW_ON_GPF 256 initial / 512-page steps)
Tested GPU: build-checked (universal Android build v6-v14); not run on a Bifrost device
Tested Kbase UAPI: none on Bifrost (JM 11.27/11.35/11.38 seen in logs)
Mesa base range: 5a07217f + g615-v11-csf series + jm-v9 001-030
Dependencies: jm-v9 001, 004, 023
Validation test: vkCreateDevice + first draw on a G52 r1 (pending); log shows
the JIT skip line and "growable BO, GROW_ON_GPF"

---
 src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
@@ -1514,7 +1514,19 @@
       .max_allocations = 255,
       .phys_pages = (128ull << 30) / kbase_kmod_page_size(),
    };
-   if (ioctl(fd, KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_JIT_INIT, &jit_init)) {
+   /* Bifrost (arch < 9) JM: nothing we allocate needs JIT or CUSTOM_VA
+    * (the tiler heap is a SAME_VA GROW_ON_GPF BO), and JIT_INIT fails with
+    * ENOMEM on G52 r1 kernels, so skip it (as JimVulkan/mali-panvk, MIT). */
+   uint64_t raw_id = kbase_gpuprop_get(props_buf, props_size,
+                                       KBASE_GPUPROP_RAW_GPU_ID, 0);
+   if (!raw_id)
+      raw_id = kbase_gpuprop_get(props_buf, props_size,
+                                 KBASE_GPUPROP_PRODUCT_ID, 0) << 16;
+   if (!is_csf && raw_id && pan_arch(raw_id & 0xffffffffu) < 9) {
+      mesa_logi("kbase: v%u JM, KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_JIT_INIT skipped; tiler "
+                "heap is a GROW_ON_GPF region",
+                pan_arch(raw_id & 0xffffffffu));
+   } else if (ioctl(fd, KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_JIT_INIT, &jit_init)) {
       mesa_logw("kbase: KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_JIT_INIT failed: %s "
                 "(tiler heap creation will not work)", strerror(errno));
    }
@@ -2047,6 +2059,16 @@
          alloc_flags |= KBASE_JM_MEM_TILER_ALIGN_TOP;
          commit_pages = MIN2(extension, va_pages);
       }
+
+      /* Bifrost JM (no JIT, see dev_create): commit 1 MiB up front and let
+       * GPU faults grow the rest in 2 MiB steps (JimVulkan/mali-panvk). */
+      if (!kbase_dev->is_csf && pan_arch(dev->props.gpu_id) < 9 &&
+          (kmod_flags & PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_MMAP)) {
+         commit_pages = MIN2((1024 * 1024) / page_size, va_pages);
+         mesa_logi("kbase: v%u growable BO, GROW_ON_GPF, %" PRIu64
+                   " of %" PRIu64 " pages committed",
+                   pan_arch(dev->props.gpu_id), commit_pages, va_pages);
+      }
    }
 
    if (kbase_dev->is_csf &&
